WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.000
An error told you nothing you could look up.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
We logged the cause. You saw a shrug.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.700
Both true. Nothing joined them.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.900
Now every failure hands you a reference.

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.100
The same characters are on the log line.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.500
The cause itself is still never returned.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.400
An id from outside is checked first.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.800
A newline would let a caller write our log.

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.400
Then it did nothing at all.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.800
Our own crate was filtered out of the log.

11
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.600
Every test passed. Only running it showed this.

12
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.400
A second reason the log was empty.

13
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.900
It writes its own line now, one per request.

14
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.500
Why logs, and not dashboards.

15
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.400
Three models leave no room. They are the product.

16
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.300
Every link in the docs now resolves.

17
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.700
One of two hundred and seventy-one did not.

18
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.000
And an hour-long path in, for anyone new.

19
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
A reported fault is now one search.
